## Summary

Ported the web `useApiHealth` hook (`web/src/api/hooks/useApiHealth.ts`) to a UI-free KMP shared-core state holder at full parity.

**What I built:**
- **`ApiHealthRepository` + `ApiHealthProbe`** (S7 port) ΓÇö a single `suspend probe()`, no cache/mutation surface (the web hook neither caches nor mutates).
- **`HttpApiHealthRepository`** ΓÇö probes `GET /healthz` at the API **root** (`versioned=false`, *not* `/api/v1`), reads the body as raw text so 2xx is judged on status alone (web `res.ok`), times the round-trip via injected `Clock`, and resolves failures to `ok=false` (never throws) ΓÇö mirroring the web `try/catch`.
- **`ApiHealth` derivation** ΓÇö pure `bucket()`/`deriveState()`: `ok` (<500ms), `degraded` (ΓëÑ500ms), `offline` (!ok), `unknown` (no probe).
- **`ApiHealthStore`** ΓÇö hot `StateFlow<ApiHealthState>` that probes immediately, re-probes every 15s (`POLL_INTERVAL_MS`), and pauses when unobserved (`WhileSubscribed` Γåö `refetchIntervalInBackground:false`). SI preserved (latency ms, ISO timestamp).
- **Golden vectors** (`spec/api-health-golden.json`, 10 scenarios incl. 499/500/501 boundaries) + cross-platform loaders (common expect + android/apple actuals) to pin KMPΓåöC# parity.
